From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: ath11k: nss: forced wifili thread scheme id (E84)

E84. With the 1/1 topology the wifili data path runs exactly one
iteration while the control path stays alive - the signature of a radio
worker thread that never gets scheduled. scheme_id has been 1 (LOW,
allocated from the DT nss-radio-priority) since E77, and the old H1a
hypothesis holds that the LOW scheme thread never runs on the single
core MP blob. The 1/1 + scheme 0 cell of the matrix was never tested.

nss_scheme=0 (default)  send scheme 0, no allocation
nss_scheme=255          the E77 behaviour, allocate from the DT
any other value         sent as-is

Not for submission - this is a measurement.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -32,6 +32,15 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(nss_rx_rel_wbm0,
 		 "hand WBM2SW0 to wifili as the rx release ring (debug)");
 
+/* DEBUG E84: thread scheme index sent in the pdev init message.
+ * 255 = allocate from nss-radio-priority in the DT (the E77 behaviour,
+ * which yields scheme 1 = LOW on this board). Any other value is sent
+ * as-is with no allocation.
+ */
+static unsigned int nss_scheme = 0;
+module_param(nss_scheme, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(nss_scheme, "wifili pdev thread scheme id, 255 = from DT (debug)");
+
 
 /* DEBUG E78: on demand dump of the DP ring state - the rings live in host
  * DMA memory and the HP/TP registers are readable through ab->mem, so a
@@ -3543,7 +3552,10 @@
 	 * database maps the low priority entry to index 1, so a board with
 	 * "nss-radio-priority = 0" is meant to send 1, not 0.
 	 */
-	if (!of_property_read_u32(dev->of_node, "nss-radio-priority",
+	if (nss_scheme != 255) {
+		/* DEBUG E84: forced scheme index, no allocation */
+		scheme_id = nss_scheme;
+	} else if (!of_property_read_u32(dev->of_node, "nss-radio-priority",
 				  &nss_radio_priority)) {
 		scheme_id = nss_wifili_thread_scheme_alloc(ab->nss.ctx,
 							  ar->nss.if_num,
